{\fs34{\b KABIR DATTANI}}\par
{\f1\fs20 Wedding photography, based in Assagao, Goa. Shooting across India since 2014.\cf1\fs20\par}
\cf0\f0\fs22
\par
{\b\fs26 A note on how I work\fs22\par}
I photograph weddings the way a documentary photographer would, if a documentary photographer were allowed to say "please look at each other for ten seconds". Forty-two percent of my frames come from the two minutes nobody rehearsed: the uncle arguing with the caterer, the flower girl asleep under the mandap, the groom\'92s hands shaking while he folds his own dhoti. I stay out of the way for nine hours of a fourteen-hour day, then I ask for the thirty minutes that are mine.\par
I have shot 186 weddings in eleven seasons, in 14 states, in four languages I do not speak. I have never lost a card. I have twice lost a moment to a bad vantage point, and both times I told the couple about it the next morning, because a photograph you cannot get is cheaper to admit than a story you invent at delivery.\par
\par
{\b\fs26 Packages\fs22\par}
{\b 1. The Single Day (10 hours, one photographer).} Rs. 1,28,000. One wedding day, 320 to 380 delivered images, colour graded. Print release included. My most booked package, and the right one for functions under 250 guests.\cf2\fs20\par
\cf0
{\b 2. Two Functions, Two Days.} Rs. 2,14,000. Mehendi or haldi plus the wedding, or the wedding plus the reception. Two photographers on the larger day, 550 to 640 delivered images, one 25-minute film cut from the second day\'92s footage.\cf2\fs20\par
\cf0
{\b 3. The Full Story (3 to 5 days).} Rs. 3,95,000 to Rs. 5,40,000 depending on the day count. Everything from the ganpati ceremony to the farewell lunch, two bodies and two assistants throughout, 900 to 1,400 delivered frames, a 6 to 9 minute film, and a 30-page hand-bound album on cotton rag paper.\cf2\fs20\par
\cf0
{\b 4. Elopement / Two-Person Wedding.} Rs. 76,000. Five hours, one location within 60 km of Panaji, 120 frames, next-week delivery. Popular with couples who want one good morning and no band.\cf2\fs20\par
\cf0
{\b 5. Post-Wedding Portraits.} Rs. 92,000. A separate golden-hour session, usually two to five days after the function, at a beach or a spice plantation near Ambigad. 150 frames, retouched, and the couple\'92s favourite two images printed at 12x18 and handed over in person.\cf2\fs20\par
\cf0
{\b 6. Reception-Only Coverage.} Rs. 64,000. Four hours, evening only, one photographer, 140 frames delivered in three days. Useful when the wedding day was covered by a local team and the reception is the one the parents actually paid for.\cf2\fs20\par
\cf0
{\i Add-ons:} second photographer Rs. 18,000 per day; 40-page album Rs. 34,000; drone only where permission is pre-arranged, Rs. 22,000; candid-plus-traditional second shooter Rs. 26,000. Travel outside Goa at actual cost, usually Rs. 9,000 to Rs. 26,000 per trip including flights and one night\'92s stay, billed with receipts and never marked up.\par
Booking holds a date with 30 percent; the balance is due seven days before the first function. Dates within the November\'97January window go 4 to 7 months ahead.\par
\par
{\b\fs26 Gear, files and delivery\fs22\par}
Two Sony bodies (A7 IV and an A7C II as a quiet second), a 35mm f/1.4, 50mm f/1.2, 85mm f/1.4 and a 24\'9670 for the wide chaos of a baraat. Godox V106 flash, always bounced, never pointed at a face. I still carry a Contax 645 and shoot two rolls of Portra 400 on every wedding, for the couple\'92s portraits only; the grain in those frames does something no preset manages. Dual card slots write simultaneously. Cards are copied to two SSDs on the evening of the shoot and kept unedited for 90 days. Editing happens in Lightroom, my colour call, no face-liquefaction unless you ask in writing. Delivery: 20 preview images within 72 hours, full gallery in 6 to 9 weeks, hosted on a private page for one year plus a downloadable archive.\par
\par
